  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "Two tangents are drawn from a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;to the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, such that the angle between these tangents is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math> If the centre of the circle is denoted by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> and these tangents touch the circle at points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>, then the ratio of the areas of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is :",
    "image": null
  },
