  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let, the angle between the tangents <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;from the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;to the circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;with centre&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>We know that&nbsp;the centre and radius of a circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>f</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;are respectively&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi></msqrt><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Thus, the centre and radius of the circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;are respectively&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;unit.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ff8cc8d3-4c00-41db-b2c8-f4fc79558a35-image.png\" style=\"width: 275px; height: 225px;\" /></p><p>We know that the line joining the centre of a circle to the point of contact of the tangent is perpendicular to the tangent, hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;also&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;bisects the angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8773;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>S</mi></math>&nbsp;congruency.</p><p>Thus, we have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>In&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;we have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p>Since, tangents to a circle from an external point are equal, hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></math></p><p>Area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>c</mi><mi>o</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p>Using&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;we get</p><p>Area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p>We have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>13</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>13</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>13</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>13</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>13</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>18</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>13</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>27</mn><mn>26</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;sq units.</p><p>And, area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>13</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>13</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;sq units.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8756;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>o</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>o</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>27</mn><mn>26</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>13</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></p>",
